Azure Virtual Private Networks (VPN) (Summary)

An Azure VPN allows you to securely connect your on-premises network or devices to Azure over the internet.

Key Points:
            Uses encryption to protect data
            Connects Azure VNets to external networks
            Works over the public internet
            Types of VPN Connections:

Site-to-Site (S2S)
Connects an entire on-premises network to Azure
Always on
Used by organizations connecting their data center to Azure

Point-to-Site (P2S)
Connects a single device (e.g. laptop) to Azure
On-demand connection
Used by remote users

VNet-to-VNet
Connects two Azure VNets together securely
Used for communication between Azure networks

Required Component:
                    VPN Gateway
                    A service in Azure that enables VPN connectivity
When to Use VPN:
                Secure communication over the internet
                Lower cost than private connections
                Quick to set up
